{%- comment -%}
  Read-it-first — the sample link, at the decision point.

  WHY THIS EXISTS. The store has no reviews, and for this audience that matters less than
  it looks: people with OCD are, by definition, not reassured by other people's certainty.
  Testimony is the weakest possible proof for a reader whose whole condition is doubt
  about whether a claim applies to them.

  Demonstration is the strong form, and this shop already has it — four real pages, no
  email, no signup. On the live page that link sat about 115KB of HTML below the Add to
  cart button, which on a phone is several thousand pixels past the only moment it was
  needed. This puts it directly under the button, as the answer to "how do I know this is
  any good" at the instant the question is being asked.

  IT IS A SECOND DOOR, NOT A LOUDER ONE. The button stays the primary action and keeps
  its colour; this is quiet, bordered, secondary. Someone ready to spend $3 is not slowed
  down by it, and someone who was about to leave gets something to do other than leave.

  NO URGENCY, NO COUNTDOWN, NO "12 PEOPLE ARE VIEWING". Those are the standard conversion
  levers and every one of them is wrong here: they work by manufacturing exactly the
  anxious pressure this product exists to unwind, and the store's own copy already
  refuses them. Nothing in this block expires, counts down, or claims an audience.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign accent = block.settings.accent | default: '#39FF14'
  assign url = block.settings.sample_url
-%}

{%- if url != blank -%}
  <div class="smf" style="--smf-accent:{{ accent }};" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
    <p class="smf__lead">{{ block.settings.lead | escape }}</p>

    <a
      class="smf__link"
      href="{{ url }}"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener"
    >
      {{- block.settings.cta | escape -}}
      <span class="smf__arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    </a>

    {%- if block.settings.note != blank -%}
      <p class="smf__note">{{ block.settings.note | escape }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- style -%}
    .smf {
      margin: 10px 0 2px;
      padding: 12px 14px;
      border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 18%, transparent);
      border-radius: 12px;
      color: inherit;
    }

    .smf__lead {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: .88rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      line-height: 1.35;
    }

    /*
      Underline rather than a second filled button. Two solid buttons stacked is the
      classic way to lose a primary action — whatever the shopper came to do stops
      looking like the obvious thing to do.
    */
    .smf__link {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: baseline;
      gap: 6px;
      margin-top: 6px;
      min-height: 44px;
      align-content: center;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      font-size: .88rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--smf-accent);
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-underline-offset: 3px;
    }
    .smf__link:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid currentColor; outline-offset: 2px; }
    .smf__arrow { text-decoration: none; }

    .smf__note {
      margin: 2px 0 0;
      font-size: .76rem;
      line-height: 1.45;
      opacity: .62;
    }
  {%- endstyle -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Read it first",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Puts the free sample directly under the Add to cart button, as the answer to \"how do I know this is any good\"."
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "sample_url",
      "label": "Sample file",
      "info": "Leave empty and the block does not render."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "lead",
      "label": "Lead line",
      "default": "Not sure yet? Read it before you buy it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "cta",
      "label": "Link text",
      "default": "Read four real pages, free"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "note",
      "label": "Note",
      "default": "Actual pages from the workbooks. No email, no signup, opens in a new tab."
    },
    { "type": "color", "id": "accent", "label": "Accent colour", "default": "#39FF14" }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Read it first" }]
}
{% endschema %}
